    "body": "BLOCKED: This issue assumes a working web client and a generic backend query API already exist and only needs a new registered view added. Neither exists yet, and building them is outside what a \"responsive mailbox client shell\" issue can decide on its own.\n\n**What I verified directly (not just inferred):**\n\n1. **`web/` is a true empty scaffold.** It contains only `README.md` and `review-rules/`. `web/review-rules/context.md` states explicitly: *\"The codebase is currently an empty scaffold — no framework has been chosen yet... These rules apply from the first real implementation PR onward.\"* `git log -- web/` shows zero feature commits, ever. So #96 would be the very first web implementation PR — yet its body asks me to \"follow the existing client tokens, i18n, loading, empty, and error conventions,\" none of which exist anywhere in the repo (no `cs.json`/`en.json`, no design-token file, no component library, no test setup).\n\n2. **No transport layer exists between any client and the backend.** `packages/realtime/src/wsServer.ts` is a one-way LISTEN/NOTIFY change-broadcast only, and its own doc comment says *\"the caller owns `wss` (and whatever HTTP server it's attached to)\"* — but no HTTP server exists anywhere in this repo (`express()`/`fastify(`/`app.listen` all return zero hits outside one unrelated test file). There is no request/response channel at all for a browser to call `listItems`, `queryView`, or anything else in the choke point.\n\n3. **No public generic API exists to read items across a relation.** `ChokePoint`'s public surface (`backend/packages/data/src/chokePoint/chokePoint.ts`) only exposes `createRelation`/`deleteRelation` — writes, not reads. The actual relation-read helpers (`listRelationsForItem`, `otherSide` in `relationsStore.ts`) aren't even exported from the package's `index.ts`, and the view filter DSL (`filterTree.ts`/`filterCompiler.ts`) has no relation-type filter node. \"Filter through the Emails-to-Folders relation... use generic query/item operations\" has no existing generic path to call today, in-process or otherwise.\n\n4. **No `read`/unread field exists on Emails.** `backend/packages/data/src/mail/search.ts` has a standing comment: *\"there is no read/flags property anywhere in this issue's scope... belongs to whichever issue adds a 'mark as read' UI action.\"* #96 explicitly puts \"triage shortcuts\" out of scope (that's #97, \"Add mailbox triage interactions\"), so the \"unread counts\" acceptance criterion has no backing data field and no in-scope way to add one here.\n\n**Why I'm not building these myself:** picking a web framework, designing and exposing an authenticated HTTP/WS API surface over the choke point, and adding a public generic relation-read method are irreversible architectural and security decisions that affect the whole `web/` platform going forward, not just this view. They're well beyond \"no new abstraction... beyond what the current issue's Zadani asks for,\" and getting the auth/transport model wrong here would be expensive to unwind later.\n\n**What a human needs to decide:**\n- Pick the web framework/build tooling for `web/` (or confirm this issue is meant to make that call).\n- Decide how the web client is authenticated and how it reaches the backend (new HTTP API? attach to the existing `packages/realtime` WS connection? something else) — and whether that's in scope for #96 or should be its own preceding issue.\n- Decide whether a public generic relation-read method should be added to `ChokePoint`/exported from `packages/data`, as part of #96 or as a preceding backend issue.\n- Decide where the Emails `read`/unread property is introduced, given #96 needs to *read* an unread count but #97 owns \"mark as read\" triage actions.\n\nLeaving this issue open rather than merging a partial/simulated implementation.",
